Helios DXVK fork: record VK_EXT_image_drm_format_modifier support

Conduit guest/windows/docs/shared-formats.md sections 9 and 10. Applied
after 0012 by ci/windows/Build-Driver.ps1.

0001 (Venus ForeignImport) and 0010 (NVK explicit LINEAR import) enable
VK_EXT_image_drm_format_modifier in enableFeaturesAndExtensions when the
device supports it. The extension is deliberately left out of the feature
list (enabling it on every device changed ordinary OPTIMAL import
requirements, the .38 regression), but initSupportedExtensions records
support only for feature-list entries, so its spec version stayed 0: no
device ever enabled it, and every import of a LINEAR foreign surface (a
KMD GDI texture in RM video memory) took the rebuild path and failed with
"DxvkImage: failed to allocate backing storage" (369.1: drm_modifier_ext=0
on every NVK device, with NVK patch 0042 advertising the extension).
Support is now recorded; enabling stays as 0001 and 0010 have it.

diff --git a/src/dxvk/dxvk_device_info.cpp b/src/dxvk/dxvk_device_info.cpp
index 9b16e980..33a41aa6 100644
--- a/src/dxvk/dxvk_device_info.cpp
+++ b/src/dxvk/dxvk_device_info.cpp
@@ -388,6 +388,20 @@ namespace dxvk {
           f.extensionSupported->specVersion = std::max(1u, iter->specVersion);
       }
     }
+
+    // Helios: VK_EXT_image_drm_format_modifier is deliberately not in the
+    // feature list (enabling it on every device changed ordinary OPTIMAL
+    // import requirements, the .38 regression), so the loop above never
+    // records its support, and enableFeaturesAndExtensions, which turns it on
+    // only for a ForeignImport Venus device or an NVK device, always saw spec
+    // version 0: no device ever enabled it and no explicit-modifier import
+    // ran. Record the support here; enabling stays where it was.
+    { auto& drm = m_extensionsSupported.extImageDrmFormatModifier;
+      auto iter = std::lower_bound(extensions.begin(), extensions.end(), drm, vk::SortExtension());
+
+      if (iter != extensions.end() && !vk::SortExtension()(drm, *iter))
+        drm.specVersion = std::max(1u, iter->specVersion);
+    }
   }
 
 
